    "Fragmented Memories": {tip:"Restore the master control and singing bowl, then bring a tranquil yellow salamander to the Moksha device at Orthen.",loc:"Orthen Dig Site",req:"108 Archaeology (boostable), 86 Hunter (boostable), Know Thy Measure",items:["Master control", "Singing bowl", "Small fishing net", "Rope"],rewards:["56,500 Archaeology XP"],steps:["Study the Moksha device in the Moksha ritual site to uncover this mystery.", "Excavate a master control (damaged) from the Moksha device excavation hotspots on the platform in the centre. Alternatively, completing the Mind Your Head research will reward a damaged master control.", "Excavate a singing bowl (damaged) from the Aughra remains excavation hotspots in the south-west.", "Restore both artefacts.", "Inspect the central platform in the middle with the restored master control in the backpack.", "Proceed through the dialogue and select 'Yes' when it prompts you to place the master control on the device.", "Solve the signal strength puzzle three times.", "Inspect the Moksha device (the central platform) again and select 'Yes' when prompted.", "Set-trap on the young tree with a rope and small fishing net in the backpack to catch yellow salamanders. The salamanders are located a short way south west from the ritual site.", "Check the net trap with a restored singing bowl in the backpack to obtain a tranquil yellow salamander.", "Return to the Moksha ritual site and inspect the Moksha device (the central platform) with the tranquil yellow salamander in the backpack to solve the mystery."]},
